{
  "feature_id": "PC-202",
  "story": "Title: Trim spaces around a pet type name\n\nStory: As a clinic administrator, I want spaces before and after a pet type name to be removed when I add or rename a pet type, so that the list does not show the same type twice with different spacing.\n\n**Requires a new or changed contract from:** None\n\nExpected behaviour:\n- When a pet type is added (`POST /api/pettypes`), spaces at the start and end of `name` are removed before it is saved. The response returns the trimmed name.\n- When a pet type is renamed (`PUT /api/pettypes/{petTypeId}`), spaces at the start and end of `name` are removed before it is saved.\n- Spaces inside a name are kept (`\"guinea pig\"` stays `\"guinea pig\"`).\n- A name with no spaces around it is saved exactly as sent.\n- A `null` name is handled exactly as it is today. This story adds no new validation and no new error responses.\n- The API contract (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`) does not change.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- AC1: `POST /api/pettypes` with `\"name\": \"  hamster  \"` returns 201 and the returned pet type has `\"name\": \"hamster\"`.\n- AC2: `PUT /api/pettypes/{petTypeId}` with `\"name\": \"  dog \"` returns 204 and the pet type is saved with the name `\"dog\"`.\n- AC3: `POST /api/pettypes` with `\"name\": \"guinea pig\"` returns 201 and the returned name is `\"guinea pig\"`.\n- AC4: The existing pet type controller tests still pass, with new tests for AC1 to AC3.\n\nIn scope:\n- `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/PetTypeRestControllerV1.java` (the add and update methods).\n- Tests in `src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/PetTypeRestControllerV1Tests.java`.\n\nOut of scope: `openapi.yml`, the model and repository classes, the database schemas, every other controller, the Angular front end.",
